51. Final Exam Rules ⭐

Memorize these 10 lines:

Objects → Heap
Instance variables → Heap, inside objects
Local variables → Stack
Method parameters → Stack frame
Local reference → Stack
Referenced object → Heap
Method code → Method Area/class-level runtime data
Static variable → class-level/shared storage; commonly taught as Method Area
Instance method has this; static method doesn't
PC Register tracks the current instruction
And the most important distinction:

Method Area stores the method's class-level information/code. Stack stores the execution of that method. Heap stores the objects being operated on.